  "body": "Replaces #482 by @mkinney (their commits kept as authored) with main merged in - the fork refuses maintainer pushes. #476's fixture-mesh commits are already on main (merged 2026-11-09), so this lands only #482's own changes (`git diff origin/main --stat`: #482's 21 files plus the new test, no snapshot PNGs).\n\n## Resolution\n- main (487cf45e) merged cleanly over the contributor's own upstream merge (7c5bcf90). That merge had already resolved tree_menu.rs and state.rs by keeping both sides, and had moved #388's per-setup spindle into the shared check.\n- posting.rs: `fixture_findings` calls #482's shared `fixture_struck::op_hits`. It judges each op against **its own setup's machine spindle** (`machine::of_setup(world, op.setup)`, #388), not the global or active machine. `struck_by` (the viewport tint) goes through `op_hits` too, so the tint and the post gate agree. Nothing in fixture_struck.rs or fixture_view.rs reads the global machine. The table box already comes from `fixture::table_box(world, setup)`, which uses `of_setup`. No `spindle_of` is left over in posting.rs.\n\n## New pinning test\n`crates/app/tests/fixture_ux.rs::the_struck_check_judges_each_op_on_its_own_setups_spindle`: two setups on mills with a 300 mm and a 20 mm spindle housing run the same face pass next to the same tall clamp, standing 60 mm off. `fixture_findings`, `op_hits` and `struck_by` convict the op in the big-housing setup and clear the one in the small-housing setup. The small setup is the active one, so a global-machine read would clear both. A mutation check confirms it: swapping `op_hits` to `machine::of(world)` fails the test.\n\n## Targeted gate (green)\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test fixture_ux --test fixture_mesh --test fixtures --test posting --test setup_mounts_post`: 9 + 3 + 14 + 17 + 5 passed.\n- From `crates/ui`, `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- fixture tree_menu`: 9 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nNot exercised: the hands-on GUI check #482 notes.\n\nChangelog: Fixtures: mark or import a fixture from the browser, see whether each fixture is judged by its mesh or only its box (and why), and see which fixture a warned move strikes (#339)\n\nRefs #339\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
